A||N||7||pherder||IT LIVES!!!!!  (long)||||10||
Z||000000||pherder||08-05-2000||02:53 PM||||Today, after 3 plus years of working on my 88 Coupe, I have had the HO Quad 4 engine fired up and running!!!!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I had spark, compression, fuel pressure, oil pressure, fuel pump would run the 2 seconds after turning the key on and then would run when the oil pressure was up, and had an noid light on every injector which would light up but it wouldn't fire.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Pulled off the injector rail and had the wife crank over the engine while I looked at the injectors ... hmmmmm?  no fuel ...<P>Had another set of injectors (off a LO Quad 4 engine) and thought, what the $!@# and swapped them out.  I turn over the engine and HAVE FUEL SQUIRTING OUT!!!!  Attempt to reinstall the fuel rail with the "new" injectors ... ain't gonna go ... drop out the engine assembly (for the 13th time ... yes, I really mean 13 times the engine assembly has been removed or installed) and proceeded to reinstall everything on the engine (MUCH easier this way   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )  Reinstall (now the 14th time) and turn the key to try to start the car ... it spins over but no fire   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  WAIT!!!  I forgot to put the sparkplug boots back on (Q4 doesn't use spark plug wires but has a boot that plugs into the coil pack and that plugs into the spark plug)!!!  Get them on and try again ... spins and coughs!!!!!  Must have the coil packs wired up backwards (i.e. 1 and 4 fire together and 2 and 3 fire together so I must have them reversed).  I then disconnect the IDI cover,  and set up upside down on the engine and take a set of Fiero V6 spark plug wires and run them from the coil pack to the spark plugs (reversing the 1-4 with the 2-3) and get try again to see if it will run.  <P>Turn the key, fuel pump runs and stops ... turn the key further (to start) and the engine turns over AND RUNS!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!<P>WOOHOO!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>I then remove the coil pack and disassemble the coil wiring so that I can swap which wire goes to which coil.  Complete that and bolt down the IDI cover on the sparkplugs and try again ... yup, it still runs!<P>Now I can start doing things like hooking up the coolant lines and putting coolant into the engine, put on the suspension, and finish up getting the car back together!!<P>Any bets on what the next problem will be on this car to keep me from driving it?  I am betting on the slave cylinder of the FWD Isuzu transaxle will not disengage the clutch.  I have a bigger clutch master cylinder incase the stock Fiero's clutch master cylinder doesn't move enough fluid to push the clutch slave cylinder's pushrod far enough.<P>For now, I am taking a break ...<P>Paul<BR>--<BR>88 Coupe, 88 Formula, 88 GT<BR>Sedgwick, KS<BR>pherder@kscable.com<p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 08-05-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000001||My7Fieros||08-05-2000||05:07 PM||||Glad to hear you got her up and running man! Undoubtably yes, you'll prob. have a few more problems before its all said and done, (after all, they are Fieros)but when the final adjustment is made, and shes running right.....well, It'll be worth it!<BR>Oh yeah, btw...PICS PICS PICS!!!!! I want to see some pics!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000002||mrfixit58||08-05-2000||05:20 PM||||GREAT NEWS! Weren't you close to selling the car because you were about to give up! There is almost nothing more satisfing then having a project finally start to come together. Congratulations!<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000003||pherder||08-05-2000||05:52 PM||||Actually, I have someone coming up tonight to look over all the Fiero stuff I have ...<P>As for pictures ... they are @ PhotoPoint ... <BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=208525&a=1537447" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=208525&a=1537447</A> <P>I have found two things wrong that will have to be fixed ... the MAP is setting a code 33 (MAP voltage high) and I believe it is a wiring problem  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Second thing is what I thought would happen ... clutch will not release.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Got the scare of my life a little while ago.  Was running the engine and my fire alarm went off ... "FIRE! ... FIRE! LEAVE THE BUILDING NOW!!!"  It got my attention.  It was the exhaust setting it off since I didn't have any fire external to the engine!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfixit58||08-05-2000||09:22 PM||||Paul,<P>So... does that mean that your selling the Q4 coupe??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Hope not,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000005||pherder||08-05-2000||10:42 PM||||Roy, <P>He came, he saw and he told me he is also thinking about getting out of the Fiero hobby (and into Corvettes!) so no sale there.<P>I have way over $30,000 tied up in my three 88 Fieros, a V8Archie install kit (and engine and other parts along with it), a P.I.S.A. Artero kit, and a bunch of other Fiero odds and ends.  I would sell it all for $15,000!!! to get out of the Fiero hobby also.  I am getting real tired of working on them all the time without having any fun driving them.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Looks like I have to drop out the engine/transaxle assembly out of the 88 Coupe again.  Wiring problems to the MAP.  I have 5 volt reference voltage all the time from the MAP and it sets a code 33.  TS to wiring problems (since it has been the same for all the different ECMs I have used in it (5 at last count), it has to be a wiring problem.)  <P>AND I can't get the clutch to work so I will be putting on the Wilwood master cylinder and hoping it will push enough fluid AND that the slave works at all!<P>Paul  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||My7Fieros||08-05-2000||11:28 PM||||Sounds like alot of time, effort, and money to just sell it all and "get out of the hobby"...<BR>But these cars are addictive...you'll be back  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000007||Eric_PA||08-05-2000||11:58 PM||||Congrats Paul on getting that Quad running. I am planning on doing my Quad swap this fall. I'm not going to mess with the coil packs at first to make the cover face the right way. I will down the road. I was wondering how you mounted the engine on the right side. Did you use a kit? I talked to you a while back about the swap when you couldn't get it running. Also, do you know if it will outperform a stock 2.8 in the fiero. I hope it does cause I allready have the engine to replace my current V6. Great Exhaust setup!!!<P>Eric<p>[This message has been edited by Eric_PA (edited 08-06-2000).]||||reg||1
